  routes=[
   dict(key="mumbai", to="Mumbai", km=1370, days="5 to 7 days", road="Via Jhansi, Indore and Nashik",
    intro="This is one of the oldest migration routes out of Uttar Pradesh, carrying professionals, traders and families from Lucknow to jobs and relatives in Mumbai, Thane and Navi Mumbai.",
    about="The truck leaves Lucknow on NH27 towards Kanpur and Jhansi, then heads south-west through Shivpuri, Guna and Dewas to Indore. From Indore it follows the old Agra-Mumbai road down to the Narmada crossing at Khalghat, on to Dhule and Nashik, and through the Kasara ghat into Thane and Mumbai. The road distance is about 1,370 km, which places this move in the 500 to 1,500 km band, the middle band of our chart. A shared truck usually delivers in 5 to 7 days from the day of loading.",
    dest="Almost everyone moving from Lucknow to Mumbai ends up with less space. A spacious independent house in Gomti Nagar or a 3 BHK in Sushant Golf City often becomes a 1 BHK or 2 BHK in Andheri, Malad, Thane or Kharghar, so deciding early what to sell, gift or store keeps the load and the bill down. Mumbai housing societies usually want a written approval from the secretary before a truck is allowed in, and many fix the shifting hours. From June to September the rain is heavy and constant, so unloading is planned with covers for the entrance and the lift.",
    tip="Get the floor plan of your Mumbai flat before the survey in Lucknow. With the room sizes in hand, the surveyor can tell you which pieces will fit, and you avoid paying to carry a large diwan or dining table 1,370 km only to sell it on arrival.",
    faqs=[("How many days does Lucknow to Mumbai shifting take?","Usually 5 to 7 days on a shared truck from loading, and less on a dedicated vehicle. In December and January fog on the first stretch through Uttar Pradesh can add a day. The coordinator shares the driver's number on the loading day."),
          ("Can you deliver to Thane, Navi Mumbai or Mira Road?","Yes. Thane, Navi Mumbai nodes such as Kharghar, Vashi and Panvel, and the western suburbs up to Mira Road and Vasai are delivered on the same 500 to 1,500 km chart. Tell us the society's move-in rules early, because some need a few days' notice."),
          ("What does a bike cost from Lucknow to Mumbai?","A scooter costs about Rs 3,500 to 5,500, a bike up to 150cc about Rs 4,000 to 6,000, a 150cc to 350cc bike about Rs 5,500 to 8,000 and a premium bike above 350cc about Rs 8,000 to 11,500 on this route, plus GST.")],
    photos=["crew/crew-paper-wrap-taping", "sp/sp-team-truck-1200", "crew/crew-wrapped-furniture", "crew/crew-carton-taping"],
    more=[
     ("Who moves from Lucknow to Mumbai", [
       "The Lucknow to Mumbai route has carried people for generations, and it still does. Young professionals take jobs in banking, media, advertising and the film industry; traders and small business owners open shops or offices in the suburbs; and many families move to join sons and daughters already settled in Thane or Navi Mumbai. There are also plenty of returning moves the other way, which means trucks run regularly in both directions and shared loads are easy to arrange.",
       "Home shifting from Lucknow to Mumbai usually starts in a house rather than a flat. Families in Indira Nagar, Aliganj or Mahanagar may have lived in the same place for twenty years, with heavy wooden furniture, a large fridge, a steel almirah in every room and boxes of books. Sorting these before the survey, and deciding what goes to relatives in Lucknow, makes the biggest difference to the estimate. A clear list also helps the surveyor size the truck correctly the first time."]),
     ("Packing a Lucknow home for Mumbai's rain and small lifts", [
       "Goods leaving a dry Lucknow summer can be unloaded into a Mumbai downpour, so mattresses go into thick plastic covers, sofas and beds are wrapped in corrugated sheet and stretch film, and cartons of clothes and books are lined with plastic before sealing. Steel almirahs get extra padding at the corners, because scratches and damp together lead to rust. Traditional brass and copper utensils are wrapped individually so they do not dent each other on the ghat roads.",
       "Many Mumbai lifts are too small for a large wardrobe, a diwan or a dressing table with a fixed mirror. These pieces are dismantled in Lucknow, with screws and fittings bagged and taped to the furniture, so the Mumbai partner team can reassemble them inside the flat. Every carton is numbered, marked with its room and listed on the inventory sheet, which you sign at loading and again at delivery, so a missing box shows up at once."]),
     ("Lucknow to Mumbai shifting charges, worked out", [
       "On the 500 to 1,500 km band, a 1 RK from Lucknow to Mumbai costs about Rs 13,000 to 23,000, a 1 BHK about Rs 15,000 to 27,000, a 2 BHK about Rs 20,000 to 36,000 and a 3 BHK about Rs 26,000 to 46,000, all plus GST. A large 4 BHK house is about Rs 34,000 to 58,000 plus GST. A compact SUV on a carrier costs about Rs 12,000 to 19,000 plus GST and a luxury car in an enclosed carrier about Rs 28,000 to 45,000 plus GST. Tolls, any extra floors without a lift and storage at the Mumbai end are separate lines on the estimate."])]),
   dict(key="pune", to="Pune", km=1365, days="5 to 7 days", road="Via Indore, Dhule and Nashik",
    intro="Students heading to Pune's colleges, IT staff joining Hinjewadi and Kharadi, and engineers bound for the Chakan auto belt make up most of the moves on this route.",
    about="From Lucknow the truck takes NH27 through Kanpur to Jhansi, crosses into Madhya Pradesh past Shivpuri and Guna, and reaches Indore by way of Dewas. South of Indore it descends to the Narmada at Khalghat, enters Maharashtra near Shirpur and continues to Dhule, then takes the Nashik side and the Nashik-Pune highway through Sangamner and Chakan into Pune. The road distance is about 1,365 km, so this move is priced in the 500 to 1,500 km band of our chart. Household goods on a shared truck usually arrive in 5 to 7 days.",
    dest="Most Pune addresses for people from Lucknow are in the western and eastern IT belts: Hinjewadi, Wakad, Baner and Balewadi on one side, and Kharadi, Viman Nagar, Wagholi and Hadapsar on the other. These are largely gated high-rise societies that ask for a move-in form, a copy of the rent agreement, a security pass for the truck and a booked lift. Pune's monsoon from June to September brings frequent rain but rarely the flooding Lucknow sees, and its winters are mild. Traffic around Hinjewadi at office hours is heavy, so unloading is usually set for mid-morning or late evening.",
    tip="If you are a student moving into a PG or hostel near your Pune college, check the room size and what furniture is already provided before you pack. Many PGs come with a bed and cupboard, and sending only cartons, a study table and a bike keeps the load to a 1 RK.",
    faqs=[("How long does shifting from Lucknow to Pune take?","Plan for 5 to 7 days on a shared truck from the loading day. A dedicated truck can reach in 3 to 4 days at a higher price. The coordinator gives you the driver's number and tells you early if the date moves."),
          ("Can a student shift from Lucknow to Pune at a low cost?","Yes. A hostel or PG load of a few cartons, a study table, a mattress and a bike is charged as a 1 RK, about Rs 13,000 to 23,000 plus GST on this route. If you can wait a few extra days for a shared load, the price usually sits near the lower end."),
          ("What does a car cost from Lucknow to Pune?","On a carrier, a hatchback costs about Rs 9,000 to 15,000, a sedan about Rs 10,500 to 17,000, a compact SUV about Rs 12,000 to 19,000 and an SUV or MUV about Rs 14,000 to 22,000 on this route, plus GST. The car is photographed at pickup.")],
    photos=["crew/crew-carton-shoulder", "sp/sp-loading-720", "crew/crew-paper-wrap-taping", "crew/crew-wrapped-furniture"],
    more=[
     ("Why Lucknow families and students choose Pune", [
       "Pune draws people from Lucknow for study as much as for work. Every year engineering, management and law students leave for colleges in Pune with a room's worth of belongings, and many stay on after a campus placement in Hinjewadi, Magarpatta or Kharadi. Engineers from Uttar Pradesh also find roles in the automotive and manufacturing plants around Chakan and Talegaon, and some families move simply for Pune's milder climate after years of Lucknow summers.",
       "Because the reasons vary so much, loads on this route range from a single room to a full family house. A typical job move is a 2 BHK from a flat in Gomti Nagar Extension or along Kursi Road, often with a home office setup and a bike. Families moving a whole house from Ashiyana or Rajajipuram usually carry more furniture, and the Pune flat is often smaller, so the survey is a good moment to decide what to leave behind with relatives in Lucknow."]),
     ("Timing a Lucknow to Pune move", [
       "College sessions and job joining dates decide most moves on this route. Students usually travel in June or July, which means the truck crosses Madhya Pradesh in the hot pre-monsoon weeks and reaches Pune in the rain, so cartons are lined with plastic and mattresses are bagged. Job moves are spread across the year, but the end of each month is the busiest time, because most leases start on the first.",
       "If you can, book the truck as soon as the Pune address is fixed. A confirmed date makes it easier to book the society lift at both ends, and shared loads fill quickly at month end. For a lease that starts on the first, loading in Lucknow four or five days before usually gets the goods there on time. In December and January, allow an extra day for fog on the Kanpur and Jhansi stretch."]),
     ("Lucknow to Pune shifting charges by home size", [
       "For about 1,365 km, a 1 BHK from Lucknow to Pune costs about Rs 15,000 to 27,000, a 2 BHK about Rs 20,000 to 36,000, a 3 BHK about Rs 26,000 to 46,000 and a 4 BHK about Rs 34,000 to 58,000, plus GST. A small office of up to 10 workstations costs about Rs 40,000 to 70,000 plus GST, and a 150cc to 350cc bike about Rs 5,500 to 8,000 plus GST. The survey turns the band into one written figure, and that figure is what you pay at delivery."])]),
   dict(key="hyderabad", to="Hyderabad", km=1300, days="5 to 7 days", road="Via Kanpur, Sagar and Nagpur (NH44)",
    intro="IT, pharma and banking jobs in HITEC City, Gachibowli and the Financial District pull a growing number of Lucknow professionals and their families to Hyderabad.",
    about="The truck leaves Lucknow for Kanpur, then runs south through Bundelkhand by way of Hamirpur, Mahoba and Chhatarpur to Sagar in Madhya Pradesh. It joins NH44 at Sagar and follows it through Lakhnadon, Seoni and Nagpur, into Telangana at Adilabad, across the Godavari near Nirmal and on through Kamareddy to Hyderabad's Outer Ring Road. The road distance is about 1,300 km, so this move is in the 500 to 1,500 km band of our chart. A shared truck usually delivers in 5 to 7 days from loading.",
    dest="Most new Hyderabad addresses for people from Lucknow are in the western IT belt, in Gachibowli, Kondapur, Madhapur, Nanakramguda, Kokapet and Manikonda, with a smaller share in Kukatpally, Miyapur and Secunderabad. Many of these are large gated communities with tall towers, an association form, ID checks and a booked lift. Hyderabad's summer from March to May is hot and dry, and the rains run from June to September. The Outer Ring Road makes truck access to the western suburbs easier, but city traffic still decides the unloading hour.",
    tip="If your car will stay in Telangana for more than a year, start the re-registration paperwork early. Keep the registration certificate, insurance and pollution certificate in one folder, and ask the Lucknow transport office about the NOC before you leave.",
    faqs=[("How long does Lucknow to Hyderabad shifting take?","Usually 5 to 7 days on a shared truck from the loading day, and less on a dedicated vehicle. Fog in December and January on the Uttar Pradesh and Bundelkhand stretch can add a day, and the coordinator tells you as soon as the plan changes."),
          ("What does it cost to send a car from Lucknow to Hyderabad?","On a carrier, a hatchback costs about Rs 9,000 to 15,000, a sedan about Rs 10,500 to 17,000, an SUV or MUV about Rs 14,000 to 22,000 and a luxury car in an enclosed carrier about Rs 28,000 to 45,000 on this route, plus GST."),
          ("Can goods be delivered to Secunderabad or the eastern side of Hyderabad?","Yes. Secunderabad, Uppal, LB Nagar, Kompally and the other suburbs use the same 500 to 1,500 km chart as the IT belt. The partner team at the Hyderabad end plans the unloading time around local traffic.")],
    photos=["sp/sp-home-packing-720", "crew/crew-carton-taping", "crew/crew-wrapped-furniture", "sp/sp-loading-720"],
    more=[
     ("Who shifts from Lucknow to Hyderabad", [
       "Hyderabad has become one of the main destinations for engineering graduates from Lucknow and the rest of Uttar Pradesh. Many join IT and product companies in HITEC City and the Financial District straight after college and later bring their families. Pharma and life sciences companies add another group, and so do bank and insurance staff transferred to regional offices. Rents in the western suburbs are often lower than in Mumbai or Bengaluru for the same space, which is part of the appeal.",
       "A common load on this route is a 2 BHK from a society in Gomti Nagar Extension, Sushant Golf City or on Sultanpur Road, plus one car or bike. Families moving from independent houses in Indira Nagar or Aliganj often bring everything, because Hyderabad flats tend to be roomy. For Lucknow to Hyderabad packers and movers, a full list of furniture and appliances at the survey is what keeps the estimate close to the final bill."]),
     ("Packing for the central India heat", [
       "The road through Bundelkhand, Madhya Pradesh and Vidarbha is very hot from April to June, and the goods spend several days in that heat inside a closed truck. Candles, cosmetics, medicines and anything that can melt should travel with you. Refrigerators are defrosted and dried the day before, washing machines are drained and their drums locked, and televisions go into thick foam or their original boxes. Air conditioners taken down from a Lucknow home travel with padded outdoor units and capped copper pipes.",
       "Wooden furniture is wrapped in corrugated sheet and stretch film so that road dust does not settle in the joints or scratch the polish. Mattresses are bagged and sofas are covered on all sides. Each carton is labelled with the room it belongs to in the new flat, which saves time when the Hyderabad team unloads. Gas cylinders are not carried in the household truck, so return or transfer the connection in Lucknow before you leave."]),
     ("Lucknow to Hyderabad shifting charges", [
       "At about 1,300 km, a 1 RK from Lucknow to Hyderabad costs about Rs 13,000 to 23,000, a 2 BHK about Rs 20,000 to 36,000, a 3 BHK about Rs 26,000 to 46,000 and a 4 BHK about Rs 34,000 to 58,000, plus GST. A medium office of 10 to 30 workstations costs about Rs 80,000 to 1,50,000 plus GST. A premium bike above 350cc costs about Rs 8,000 to 11,500 plus GST. Insurance and any storage are separate lines on the estimate."])]),
   dict(key="kolkata", to="Kolkata", km=960, days="4 to 6 days", road="NH30 and NH19",
    intro="This route carries railway and central government staff, bank officers, students and many families with roots in Bengal and Bihar between the capitals of Uttar Pradesh and West Bengal.",
    about="Trucks usually leave Lucknow on NH30 through Raebareli to Prayagraj and join NH19, the old Grand Trunk Road, there. The highway runs east past Varanasi and Mughalsarai, crosses Bihar through Sasaram and Aurangabad, passes Dhanbad in Jharkhand and enters Bengal near Asansol before Durgapur, Bardhaman and Kolkata. Some drivers take the Sultanpur road to Varanasi instead. Either way the distance is about 960 km, so this move is in the 500 to 1,500 km band of our chart. A shared truck normally delivers in 4 to 6 days.",
    dest="Kolkata offers two very different arrivals. New Town, Rajarhat and parts of Salt Lake have tall towers with lifts and society rules that feel like Gomti Nagar Extension. Older homes in north and south Kolkata are often in old buildings with steep stairs and no lift, on lanes where a big truck cannot enter, so the last stretch is done in a smaller vehicle. The city is humid for most of the year and the monsoon runs from June to September. During Durga Puja in September or October many lanes are closed for pandals, so unloading in that week needs extra planning.",
    tip="Plan around Durga Puja at the Kolkata end and Chhath on the way. In the days around both festivals traffic through Bihar and Bengal is heavy and some housing societies stop moves, so try to load a week before or after.",
    faqs=[("How many days does Lucknow to Kolkata shifting take?","Usually 4 to 6 days on a shared truck from loading. In December and January dense fog on the plains of Uttar Pradesh and Bihar can add a day, and the coordinator tells you as soon as the plan changes."),
          ("Can you deliver to Howrah, Salt Lake or New Town?","Yes. Howrah, Salt Lake, New Town, Dum Dum and the other suburbs use the same 500 to 1,500 km chart as central Kolkata. If the lane is narrow, the partner team moves goods to a smaller vehicle for the last stretch."),
          ("What does a car cost from Lucknow to Kolkata?","On a carrier, a hatchback costs about Rs 9,000 to 15,000, a sedan about Rs 10,500 to 17,000, a compact SUV about Rs 12,000 to 19,000 and an SUV or MUV about Rs 14,000 to 22,000 on this route, plus GST.")],
    photos=["sp/sp-team-truck-1200", "sp/sp-home-packing-720", "crew/crew-mattress-corrugated", "crew/crew-paper-wrap-taping"],
    more=[
     ("Who takes the Lucknow to Kolkata route", [
       "Transfers drive a large share of these moves. Railway staff, central government officers, bank employees and PSU managers move between Lucknow and Kolkata offices on postings, often with a fixed joining date and an office that reimburses the cost. Families with roots in Bengal who spent years in Lucknow go back to be near parents, and students move for colleges and coaching in Kolkata. Business families in trade and textiles also move stock and households between the two cities.",
       "Many of these households carry heavy old furniture, books and musical instruments such as a harmonium or tabla, along with framed photographs and puja items that matter far more than their price. These are wrapped in corrugated sheet, padded at every corner and listed by name on the inventory sheet. For Lucknow to Kolkata packers and movers, naming such items at the survey is what lets the team bring the right material on packing day."]),
     ("Packing for the Grand Trunk Road and Kolkata's humidity", [
       "NH19 is one of India's busiest freight roads, and a loaded truck spends several days in heavy traffic, so cartons are packed tight and stacked with the heaviest at the bottom to stop shifting on rough patches. Glass table tops and mirrors are packed between boards, and steel almirahs are padded at the corners. The fog season from mid December to January means slower driving at night, but packing stays the same.",
       "At the Kolkata end the main risk is damp. Clothes, books and documents go in plastic-lined cartons, and leather and wooden furniture is wrapped in film over corrugated sheet. Once unloaded, open the cartons within a few days and let things air, and slip silica gel sachets into boxes of papers and photo albums. Where the lane is too narrow for the truck, goods are moved to a smaller vehicle at the main road, and that transfer is shown on the estimate as its own line."]),
     ("Lucknow to Kolkata shifting charges", [
       "On the 500 to 1,500 km band, a 1 BHK from Lucknow to Kolkata costs about Rs 15,000 to 27,000, a 2 BHK about Rs 20,000 to 36,000 and a 3 BHK about Rs 26,000 to 46,000, plus GST. A 4 BHK or a full house with heavy furniture is about Rs 34,000 to 58,000 plus GST. A scooter costs about Rs 3,500 to 5,500 plus GST and a bike up to 150cc about Rs 4,000 to 6,000 plus GST. The written figure after the survey is the final price, with GST shown separately."])]),
   dict(key="bengaluru", to="Bengaluru", km=1860, days="7 to 9 days", road="NH44",
    intro="Engineers, product teams and their families make up most of this route, moving from Lucknow to the tech parks of Whitefield, Electronic City and the Outer Ring Road.",
    about="From Lucknow the truck goes south through Kanpur and Bundelkhand to Sagar, joins NH44 there and follows it almost all the way: through Lakhnadon, Seoni and Nagpur, across Telangana to Hyderabad, then south through Kurnool and Anantapur into Karnataka and Bengaluru from the north, near Devanahalli and Hebbal. The distance is about 1,860 km, which puts this move in the 1,500 km plus band, the top band of our chart. A shared truck usually takes 7 to 9 days from loading.",
    dest="Bengaluru apartment associations usually want a move-in form, a copy of the rent agreement, a booked lift and fixed move hours, and many take two or three working days to approve a slot. Large trucks face time restrictions on many city roads, and the Outer Ring Road near Marathahalli and Bellandur can hold a truck for hours, so unloading is usually set for early morning. Bengaluru is far milder than Lucknow, with no real summer heat wave, but showers are frequent from June to October, so the unloading team carries sheets to cover the lobby floor and the lift.",
    tip="Ask your Bengaluru society for its move-in rules before the truck leaves Lucknow, and keep your winter quilts in a suitcase rather than the truck. Bengaluru nights are cool enough for a light blanket, but heavy Lucknow razais can go into storage cartons at the back of the load.",
    faqs=[("How many days will my goods take to reach Bengaluru from Lucknow?","Count on 7 to 9 days after loading for a shared truck. A truck booked only for your goods is quicker and priced higher. Winter fog around Kanpur sometimes adds a day, and you hear about any change from the coordinator, not at the last minute."),
          ("What does car shifting from Lucknow to Bengaluru cost?","A Swift or i20 on a carrier is about Rs 13,000 to 22,000 plus GST, a Dzire or City about Rs 15,000 to 25,000 plus GST, and an Innova, XUV700 or Fortuner about Rs 20,000 to 34,000 plus GST. Every panel is photographed before the car is loaded."),
          ("Will my employer accept your invoice for a Bengaluru relocation?","Usually yes. The GST invoice can carry your company's name and GSTIN, with packing, transport and insurance listed separately. If the HR team uses its own quote format, send it to us and the estimate is filled in that format.")],
    photos=["sp/sp-loading-720", "crew/crew-mattress-corrugated", "crew/crew-wrapped-furniture", "crew/crew-carton-taping"],
    more=[
     ("Who moves from Lucknow to Bengaluru", [
       "Most bookings on this route follow a job. Graduates from Lucknow's engineering colleges join IT services and product companies in Bengaluru, mid-career professionals move for better roles, and couples who both work in tech often relocate together. Many come back to Lucknow a few years later to shift their parents' household to Bengaluru, which brings a very different load: a full house with old furniture instead of a single room.",
       "A young professional's move from a rented room in Aliganj or a PG near Gomti Nagar is often just a 1 RK load and a bike. A family move from a flat in Sushant Golf City or a house in Vrindavan Yojana is usually a 2 BHK or 3 BHK with a car. Both loads are priced from one 1,500 km plus chart for Lucknow to Bengaluru packers and movers; the survey, the floor and the volume decide whether your figure lands near the bottom or the top of the range."]),
     ("Packing a Lucknow home for an 1,860 km trip", [
       "Goods spend a week or more on the road, through dry heat in central India and damp weather in the south. Electronics such as monitors, routers and speakers are packed in their own cartons with foam, while laptops, jewellery and documents should travel with you. Wooden furniture is wrapped in corrugated sheet and then stretch film so highway dust and Bengaluru's humidity do not reach the polish. Glass and marble table tops are packed between boards or crated.",
       "Kitchen items go into double-walled cartons with paper between plates, and pickles, ghee and oil should be packed in sealed jars inside a plastic bag or carried by hand, because a leak can spoil a whole carton over a week. Potted plants rarely survive the trip, so they are better left with neighbours. Every carton is numbered and listed on the inventory sheet, which you sign again when the Bengaluru partner team unloads."]),
     ("Lucknow to Bengaluru shifting charges, worked out", [
       "Take a typical engineer's 1 RK with a bike: the house load is Rs 18,000 to 32,000 and a Pulsar or Shine up to 150cc adds Rs 5,000 to 7,500, both before GST. A family 2 BHK sits at Rs 27,000 to 47,000 plus GST, and a big Lucknow house with four bedrooms at Rs 44,000 to 78,000 plus GST. A premium bike above 350cc, such as a Himalayan, is Rs 10,000 to 14,500 plus GST. If the Bengaluru lift is out of order or the goods need storage, that is written as a separate line, never added at the door."])]),
   dict(key="chennai", to="Chennai", km=1950, days="7 to 9 days", road="Via Nagpur, NH44 and NH16",
    intro="IT staff bound for OMR, engineers joining the auto plants around Sriperumbudur, students and families from the south returning home all use this long route from Lucknow.",
    about="Of all the routes we run from Lucknow, this one goes farthest south. The truck runs south through Kanpur and Bundelkhand to Sagar, joins NH44 at Sagar and follows it through Nagpur into Telangana, then turns south-east across Andhra Pradesh to the coast and takes NH16 through Ongole and Nellore into Chennai from the north. At roughly 1,950 km by road, Lucknow to Chennai is priced on the 1,500 km plus band. Shared loads normally reach a Chennai address 7 to 9 days after the Lucknow loading day.",
    dest="Chennai is hot and humid for most of the year, and its heaviest rain comes with the northeast monsoon from October to December, the opposite of Lucknow's July to September season. Low-lying areas such as Velachery, Pallikaranai and parts of OMR can waterlog after heavy spells, and cyclone warnings are common in November. Apartment complexes on OMR and in Porur, Medavakkam and Perungudi ask for an association form and a lift slot, while older homes in Mylapore, T Nagar and Anna Nagar can have narrow stairs and little space for a truck.",
    tip="If your move falls between October and December, keep an eye on Chennai cyclone warnings in the week of delivery. When one is forecast, the coordinator holds the truck at a safe stop and delivers once the roads are clear, so leave a day or two of slack in your plans.",
    faqs=[("How many days does Lucknow to Chennai shifting take?","Plan for 7 to 9 days on a shared truck from loading. Winter fog in Uttar Pradesh can slow the first stretch and northeast monsoon rain in Andhra Pradesh and Tamil Nadu can slow the last. You are told early if the date moves."),
          ("What is the charge for a two-wheeler from Lucknow to Chennai?","A Classic 350 or Apache in the 150cc to 350cc class is about Rs 7,000 to 10,000 plus GST, an Activa or Jupiter about Rs 4,500 to 7,000 plus GST, and a commuter bike up to 150cc about Rs 5,000 to 7,500 plus GST. A superbike goes in a wooden crate for about Rs 18,000 to 28,000 plus GST."),
          ("Will my wooden furniture survive the damp Chennai air?","Sheesham and teak pieces from a dry Lucknow home are the most at risk, so they get corrugated sheet under stretch film for the trip. Clothes and books ride in cartons lined with plastic. Once the goods are in, unpack within a few days and keep windows open, because sealed cartons trap moisture.")],
    photos=["sp/sp-team-truck-1200", "sp/sp-loading-720", "crew/crew-mattress-corrugated", "crew/crew-carton-taping"],
    more=[
     ("Who moves from Lucknow to Chennai", [
       "Chennai draws people from Lucknow in several ways. IT and back-office staff take roles on OMR, in Siruseri and around Guindy; engineers join the car and component plants on the Sriperumbudur and Oragadam side; and students move for engineering, medicine and research. Central government, railway and bank transfers add a steady share, and families from Tamil Nadu who worked in Lucknow for years often go home when children reach college or parents need care.",
       "A family going back south after a long posting often sends every room of the house, while a young engineer may send only a 1 BHK load and a scooter. In both cases home shifting from Lucknow to Chennai goes smoothly when the move-in date at the new flat is fixed first, because a truck that reaches a Chennai complex before the lift slot is booked can wait hours at the gate. The coordinator confirms the slot with the association before the truck leaves Lucknow."]),
     ("Planning a 1,950 km move", [
       "Give a cross-country move at least two or three weeks of lead time. Settle the Chennai address first, because the survey, the society slot and the delivery date all depend on it. You will probably fly or take the train and reach Chennai well before the truck, so carry a week's clothes, bedding for one night, cooking basics and all school and office papers with you. A relative or neighbour in Lucknow can hold a spare key and a copy of the item list in case the loading time shifts.",
       "Over more than 1,900 km of highway, anything with glass needs boards on both faces, and a marble dining top travels in a wooden crate. Televisions, music systems and computers go in foam, and the model and serial number of each costly item is written on the list. When the Chennai flat will only be free a week or two later, a partner warehouse can hold the goods for a separate charge that appears on the estimate. Mention this during the survey so there are no new lines at the end."]),
     ("Lucknow to Chennai shifting charges explained", [
       "Here are some sample Lucknow to Chennai shifting charges from the 1,500 km plus band, all before 18 per cent GST. A single room or studio comes to Rs 18,000 to 32,000. A 1 BHK is Rs 20,000 to 35,000 and a 3 BHK Rs 34,000 to 60,000, while a large house of four bedrooms runs from Rs 44,000 to 78,000. A compact SUV such as a Creta on a carrier adds Rs 17,000 to 28,000, and a luxury car in a closed carrier Rs 40,000 to 65,000. For a small office of up to 10 desks, budget Rs 55,000 to 90,000. Toll and insurance charges appear on their own lines."])]),
  ],
